I'm surprised no one has suggested the obvious solution - instead of
producing a random item if you wish for something non-existant, why not
just say "that item does not exist. Please try again." (Possible with an
option to get a random item, if you are so bad at spelling that you have
tried 20 times and just want to get out of the loop.) So you can try
pick-axe, pickaxe, pick axe etc. until you get it right. Also very easy
to program.


